---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import ZoomImage from '../components/ZoomImage.astro';

import watercolorVeggies from '../assets/art-images/1-watercolor-veggies.jpg';
import watercolorOthers from '../assets/art-images/watercolors.jpg';
import flowersBee from '../assets/art-images/flowers-bee.jpg';
import lilypads from '../assets/art-images/lilypads.jpg';
import pinkFlower from '../assets/art-images/pink-flower.jpg';
---

<Layout>
	<Section>
        <h1 class="title">Art I've Made</h1>
        <p>
            I've always liked doing art, but hadn't made much time for it for a long time. After taking a drawing class on a whim in Fall 2024, I've been getting back into art of all kinds. In Spring 2025, I did a two-month cohort program at the <a href="https://www.nycdrawingroom.com" target="_blank">Drawing Room</a> designed to explore a variety of media, and I've continued taking other classes there as well as working on art on my own.
        </p>
        <p>Click the image thumbnails to expand them!</p>
        <div>
            <h2>Watercolors</h2>
            <p>
                The first class I took as part of the cohort program was a watercolor class using a variety of vegetables as reference. Watercolor is tricky! I'm super happy with how the leek turned out, though.
            </p>
            <ZoomImage src={watercolorVeggies} alt="A larger watercolor painting of several vegetables and two smaller paintings of a leek and a carrot" id="watercolor-veggies" first={true} last={true} />
            <p>
                I did these paintings on my own rather than in a class - the landscape is referenced from a photo I found online, and the others are referenced from photos I took (included below! I think a couple were from the botanic gardens, and one was while I was out on a walk).
            </p>
            <ZoomImage src={watercolorOthers} alt="Four small watercolor paintings. One is of a mountainous landscape, one is of a flow, one is of flowers and a bee, and one is of lily pads" id="watercolor-others" first={true} />
            <ZoomImage src={pinkFlower} alt="A photo of a pink and red flower" id="pink-flower" />
            <ZoomImage src={flowersBee} alt="A photo of purplish flowers with a bee" id="flowers-bee" />
            <ZoomImage src={lilypads} alt="A photo of lilypads on a pond" id="lilypads" last={true} />
        </div>
        <div>
            <h2>Ceramics</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h2>Block Printing</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h2>Museum Sketches</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h2>Figure Drawing</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h2>Felting</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h2>Collage</h2>
        </div>
    </Section>
</Layout>

<style lang="scss">
.title {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-top: 0;
}
</style>
